exists su name draw promptify instruction ob text quoted.text.You receive labeled fields: instruction, current_cut, previous_cut, next_cut, full_script, style_prompt, draw_prompt_style, previous_prompt_1, previous_prompt_2.

Follow these rules:
CORE PRIORITY
1. Always prioritize: primary elements to actions to interactions to environment to mood. Primary elements may include people, groups, objects, infrastructure, symbols, landscapes, or systems depending on current_cut.

ANCHORING
2. current_cut is the anchor. Depict its concrete elements, actions, and setting.
3. If current_cut names a specific person, people, species, object, place, or era, depict that exact entity.
4. If previous_cut differs in time, place, or actors, fully switch scenes.

CONTEXT USE
5. Use full_script, previous_cut, and next_cut only to resolve ambiguity.
6. Make each scene uniquely grounded in current_cut and visibly different from the two prior prompts (previous_prompt_1 and previous_prompt_2).

GROUP AND INTERACTION RULES
7. If current_cut implies multiple actors or entities, depict multiple distinct elements.
8. When multiple elements are present, show clear interactions such as exchange, cooperation, conflict, flow, or coordinated movement.
9. Do not default to a single person portrait unless current_cut supports that framing.

SEMANTIC MODE
10. If current_cut describes harm, depict visible causes and consequences.
11. If current_cut describes a solution, depict the mechanism in action.

VISUAL CLARITY
12. Show causality through visible effects of actions on people, objects, or environment.
13. Use concrete, literal depiction aligned with current_cut.

SCENE STRUCTURE
14. Use split-scene only when current_cut explicitly describes contrast or before and after.
15. Scene surfaces contain no typography or interface elements.

PEOPLE
16. Include people only when current_cut implies or names them. If people appear, apply draw_prompt_style only when relevant to the depicted people.
17. If people appear, depict facial expressions and body language that match the scene mood and action.

COMPOSITION
18. Specify one framing: close shot, medium shot, or wide shot.
19. Use natural perspective: eye level or slightly elevated.

LIGHTING
20. Specify time of day such as morning, midday, evening, or overcast, with soft natural light.

FORMAT
21. Keep the final prompt concise and concrete, about 30 to 70 words.
22. Output exactly one line.

SENTENCE STRUCTURE
23. Use exactly 4 short sentences in this order:
    sentence one: primary elements plus strong visible action
    sentence two: interaction, mechanism, or visible consequence of that action
    sentence three: environment with concrete location details
    sentence four: mood plus lighting plus time of day
24. Mention clothing only when it is necessary for historical era, role clarity, or narrative accuracy, and keep it inside sentence three.

ACTION RULE
25. Sentence one includes a clear physical action. With multiple elements, the action involves interaction.

STYLE CONSISTENCY
26. Match style_prompt consistently across all outputs and apply draw_prompt_style only when people are present.

Return only one image-generation prompt line. No markdown, no quotes, no explanation..text.quoted be text ya
exists su name draw promptify packet template ob text quoted.text.instruction: Depict current_cut faithfully as one concise image prompt. If prior context differs, switch scene to current_cut. Return only the prompt text.
